  tp_h_name: 'Where does the nickname come from?',
  tp_name_p: "The nickname came one evening around a campfire, with travellers who loved the music in my car. Tupac was already taken. And since I never leave without my three essentials — a spare tyre, good music and a smile — they came up with the name: Tripack. It stuck.",
  tp_h_road: '20 years on the roads of Madagascar',
  tp_road_p1: "In twenty years I've driven the RN7 more times than I can count. I've crossed the Tsiribihina by ferry under a blazing sun, dug the 4x4 out of the sand between Morombe and Belo-sur-Mer, driven down to Mananjary in tropical downpours, swallowed the potholes of the RN6 up to Ambanja, changed tyres in the Ranomafana rain and waited for zebu herds in the middle of the Horombe plateau. And I've always arrived safely, with my passengers in good spirits.",
  tp_road_p2: "My philosophy is simple: in Madagascar, the road is part of the journey. I don't drive to get there fast, I drive so you can see the country. We stop when a scene catches your eye, taste fritters by the roadside, chat with people.",
